{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-error-recovery", "file": "references/multi-rejection-demo-discipline.md", "content": "# Multi-rejection discipline for demo-driven ARC

In a task with one or more incorrect submissions, an incorrect result falsifies the whole proposed generator. Do not resubmit a near-identical grid or make an evidence-free palette/coordinate tweak. Rebuild a ledger from every input-output pair, including unchanged cells, and separately test scope, geometry, mapping, and palette.

When multiple candidate grids have failed and the remaining evidence does not determine the test output, stop guessing. State internally at least two concrete hypotheses and the specific observation that distinguishes them. Request one demo only if it can supply that observation, then integrate it before the next action; never treat receiving a demo as an automatic reason for another request. Submit only when one candidate explains every pair and unambiguously yields the test grid. Keep each turn to one action-only JSON object.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/held-out/play/users/u007/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-error-recovery/references/multi-rejection-demo-discipline.md"}

